From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:02:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: defconfig: Enable the X-Powers PMIC power key driver

The power key of the X-Powers PMICs (AXP20x, AXP22x, AXP318W) reports
through axp20x-pek. Build it as a module, as the other PMIC power key
drivers are, so that a press of the key reaches user space.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the driver builds as a
module, loads and registers the power key input device.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index d6415055da45..e7bb7e6a0e25 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -549,6 +549,7 @@ CONFIG_INPUT_PM8941_PWRKEY=y
 CONFIG_INPUT_PM8XXX_VIBRATOR=m
 CONFIG_INPUT_TPS65219_PWRBUTTON=m
 CONFIG_INPUT_TPS6594_PWRBUTTON=m
+CONFIG_INPUT_AXP20X_PEK=m
 CONFIG_INPUT_PWM_BEEPER=m
 CONFIG_INPUT_PWM_VIBRA=m
 CONFIG_INPUT_RK805_PWRKEY=m
